# Libs vs core (minimal)

## `app/libs`

- Infrastructure and integrations (auth setup, db clients, queue, third-party SDK wrappers, alerting).
- Keep modules reusable and low-level.
- Do not put domain workflows here.
- Error alerts and ops notifications: use `sendErrorAlert` / `sendAlertMessage` from `#/libs/alerting/index.server` (see [alerting.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/alerting.mdc)). Do not call Telegram helpers directly in new code.

## `app/core`

- Domain/business workflows that orchestrate libs and persistence (catalog, cart, orders, payments, shipping, customers, etc.).
- Core modules may depend on libs and other core modules.
- **Do not add ecommerce domain code under `app/services`.** That directory was removed; use `app/core/*` instead.

## Dependency boundary

- `core -> libs` is allowed.
- `libs -> core` is not allowed (enforced by oxlint `no-restricted-imports` on `app/libs/**`).

## Runtime config

- App runtime config lives in `#/libs/config` (derived from root `bermooda.config.js` at module load). Do not import `#/core/config`.

## File pattern

- Prefer `*.server.js` for server-only modules in both directories.
- Use `#/*` imports and omit extensions.
- Document exported functions with JSDoc; use `@typedef` and Prisma `import()` types for domain shapes (see [jsdoc-types.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/jsdoc-types.mdc)).
